course: dictionary
lesson: 6238
title: Mockery and making a mockery of
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Mockery means laughing at someone in an unkind way, or teasing them so they feel small. «The other children's mockery made Sam feel small.» The clues are unkind and small, so mockery is teasing that hurts. Test your meaning by swapping it in: "The other children's teasing made Sam feel small." It still fits, so you are right.
explain: Mockery can also mean a bad, silly copy of something that should be fair or real. «The trial was a mockery of justice.» A real trial should be fair. The words "a mockery of justice" tell you this one only looks like justice and is not.
explain: The phrase make a mockery of means to make something seem stupid or pointless. «The rain made a mockery of our picnic plans.» The picnic was spoiled, so the rain made the plans look pointless. When you meet a phrase, read the words around it to find its meaning.
fact: Mockery means laughing at someone or something in an unkind way.
fact: «Mockery» can also mean a silly copy of something that should be fair, as in «a mockery of justice».
fact: «Make a mockery of» means to make something seem stupid or pointless.
fact: «Face mockery» means to be teased or laughed at by other people.
fact: Mockery is a form of unkindness, so it can hurt people's feelings.
exercise: «The other children's mockery made Sam feel small.» What does mockery mean here? | A quiet, sleepy afternoon | A kind and happy party | A new game with a ball | *Unkind laughing and teasing
exercise: «The trial was a mockery of justice.» What is the trial like? | A long walk in the park | A happy day out | *A bad, silly copy of a fair trial | A fair and proper hearing
exercise: «The rain made a mockery of our picnic plans.» What does make a mockery of mean? | To make something bigger | To make something quiet and calm | To make something taste better | *To make something seem stupid or pointless
test: «Mockery» is a noun. Which word could replace it in «She faced mockery from the bullies»? | Silence | Kindness | Sunshine | *Teasing
test: «The fake prize was a mockery of a real competition.» What does mockery mean here? | A happy surprise | A new sports kit | *A silly copy that is so bad it is ridiculous | A real, fair contest
exam: Maya says «make a mockery of» means to make something beautiful. What is the right meaning? | *To make something seem stupid or pointless, not beautiful | To make a new friend | To make something seem stupid or pointless | To make a cake
